  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1956-p40.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "From the first equation, \\(gt=V-V_0.\\) Therefore \\[ \\begin{aligned} S&=\\frac12(gt)t+V_0t\\\\ &=\\frac12(V-V_0)t+V_0t\\\\ &=\\frac12(V+V_0)t. \\end{aligned} \\] Solving gives \\(t=\\frac{2S}{V+V_0}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Use the first equation to replace \\(gt\\) in the second",
        "Factor \\(t\\) after writing \\(gt=V-V_0\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
